  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q6",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Simplify these ratios.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 4,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$25:35$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5:7$",
          "worked": "Divide both parts by their highest common factor, $5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}25:35&=(25\\div5):(35\\div5)\\\\&=5:7\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$100:28:4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$25:7:1$",
          "worked": "Divide all three parts by their highest common factor, $4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}100:28:4&=(100\\div4):(28\\div4):(4\\div4)\\\\&=25:7:1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$1.6:1.9$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$16:19$",
          "worked": "Multiply both parts by $10$ to obtain whole numbers.\n$$\\begin{align*}1.6:1.9&=(1.6\\times10):(1.9\\times10)\\\\&=16:19\\end{align*}$$\nThe highest common factor is $1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$0.93:0.6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$31:20$",
          "worked": "Multiply both parts by $100$, then divide by the highest common factor, $3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}0.93:0.6&=93:60\\\\&=(93\\div3):(60\\div3)\\\\&=31:20\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3}{2}:2\\dfrac{1}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3:5$",
          "worked": "Write the mixed number as an improper fraction. Both fractions have denominator $2$, so multiply both parts by $2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{2}:2\\frac{1}{2}&=\\frac{3}{2}:\\frac{5}{2}\\\\&=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\times2\\right):\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\times2\\right)\\\\&=3:5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$2.2\\text{ kg}:850\\text{ g}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$44:17$",
          "worked": "$2.2\\text{ kg}=2200\\text{ g}$. Compare in grams, then divide both parts by $50$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2200:850&=(2200\\div50):(850\\div50)\\\\&=44:17\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$6\\text{ min}:2.1\\text{ h}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1:21$",
          "worked": "$2.1\\text{ h}=2.1\\times60\\text{ min}=126\\text{ min}$. Compare in minutes, then divide both parts by $6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6:126&=(6\\div6):(126\\div6)\\\\&=1:21\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}:\\dfrac{1}{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3:2$",
          "worked": "Rewrite with lowest common denominator $6$, then multiply both parts by $6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{2}:\\frac{1}{3}&=\\frac{3}{6}:\\frac{2}{6}\\\\&=\\left(\\frac{3}{6}\\times6\\right):\\left(\\frac{2}{6}\\times6\\right)\\\\&=3:2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$25\\text{ cm}:1.1\\text{ m}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5:22$",
          "worked": "$1.1\\text{ m}=110\\text{ cm}$. Compare in centimetres, then divide both parts by $5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}25:110&=(25\\div5):(110\\div5)\\\\&=5:22\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\$1.50:80\\text{ c}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15:8$",
          "worked": "$\\$1.50=150\\text{ c}$. Compare in cents, then divide both parts by $10$.\n$$\\begin{align*}150:80&=(150\\div10):(80\\div10)\\\\&=15:8\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$600\\text{ mL}:1.5\\text{ L}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2:5$",
          "worked": "$1.5\\text{ L}=1500\\text{ mL}$. Compare in millilitres, then divide both parts by $300$.\n$$\\begin{align*}600:1500&=(600\\div300):(1500\\div300)\\\\&=2:5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q6-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{5}{8}:\\dfrac{2}{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15:16$",
          "worked": "Rewrite with lowest common denominator $24$, then multiply both parts by $24$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5}{8}:\\frac{2}{3}&=\\frac{15}{24}:\\frac{16}{24}\\\\&=\\left(\\frac{15}{24}\\times24\\right):\\left(\\frac{16}{24}\\times24\\right)\\\\&=15:16\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      }
    ]
